.TH ADAHACK 6 "2026-03-29" "AdaHack 1.0" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
adahack \- a NetHack\-inspired terminal roguelike written in Ada
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B adahack
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B adahack
is a procedurally generated, turn-based dungeon crawler.
Descend ten dungeon levels, find the legendary
.B Amulet of Yendor
on level 10, and carry it back to the surface to win.
.PP
Every level is randomly generated with rooms, corridors, locked doors,
shops, traps, secret passages, dark rooms, and increasingly dangerous
monsters.  Items found or bought can shift the odds in your favour.
.SH CONTROLS
.SS Movement
.TP
.BR h " / " \(la " (left arrow)"
Move west.
.TP
.BR j " / " \(da " (down arrow)"
Move south.
.TP
.BR k " / " \(ua " (up arrow)"
Move north.
.TP
.BR l " / " \(ra " (right arrow)"
Move east.
.TP
.BR y \ u \ b \ n
Move diagonally (NW, NE, SW, SE).
.SS Actions
.TP
.B >
Descend stairs (stand on \fB>\fP).
.TP
.B <
Ascend stairs (stand on \fB<\fP).
Ascending from level 1 while carrying the Amulet of Yendor wins the game.
.TP
.B i
Open inventory.  Press a letter to use/equip/eat the item.
.TP
.B e
Quick-eat the first food ration in your pack.
.TP
.B r
Rest one turn, recovering 1 HP (cannot rest near awake monsters).
.TP
.B R
Auto-rest until full HP or until a monster wakes nearby.
.TP
.B S
Search adjacent tiles for secret doors (costs one turn).
.TP
.B f
Fire your readied bow in a chosen direction.
.TP
.B K
Kick (then choose direction).  Can break down locked doors.
.TP
.B s
Browse the shop (stand on green \fB$\fP tile).
Press a letter to buy, \fBS\fP to sell items, \fBESC\fP to leave.
.TP
.B t
Activate ring of teleportation (if equipped).
.TP
.B D
Drop an item (choose from inventory).
.TP
.B q
Quit the game (asks for confirmation; press
.B y
to quit).
.SH ITEMS
Items are picked up automatically by walking over them.
.TP
.B $ (gold)
Currency.  Spend it at shops.
.TP
.B ) (weapon)
White = melee weapon; cyan = bow.
Wield with \fBi\fP.  Value shows attack bonus (negative = cursed).
.TP
.B / (arrow)
Ammo for a bow.  Value = count.  Consumed automatically on firing.
.TP
.B [ (armor)
Wear with \fBi\fP.  Value = defence bonus (negative = cursed).
.TP
.B ! (potion)
Drink with \fBi\fP.  Colours: blue=heal, red=strength, foul-smelling=poison,
murky=blind, sparkling=invisibility.
.TP
.B ? (scroll)
Read with \fBi\fP.  Types: identify, magic map, fireball,
enchant weapon, enchant armor, teleportation.
.TP
.B = (ring)
Wear with \fBi\fP.  Types: regeneration (+1 HP/5 turns),
invisibility (monsters ignore proximity), speed (+2 attack),
teleportation (press \fBt\fP to activate).
Rings wear out after 80\[en]200 turns and crumble to dust.
.TP
.B ( (torch)
Light with \fBi\fP.  Illuminates dark rooms (radius 6 vs default 2).
Burns for 150\[en]400 turns.
.TP
.B % (food)
Eat with \fBi\fP or \fBe\fP.  Restores HP and resets hunger.
.TP
.B ? (key)
Used automatically when walking into a matching locked door (+).
.TP
.B " (Amulet of Yendor)
Found on dungeon level 10.  Carry it back to level 1 and ascend to win.
.SH MONSTERS
.TP
.B r (rat), B (bat)
Weak but common on level 1.  Bats may blind you on a hit.
.TP
.B g (goblin), o (orc)
Mid-range threats.  Appear from level 2 onward.
.TP
.B T (troll)
Tough and regenerates 1 HP every 5 turns.
.TP
.B D (dragon)
Most dangerous monster.  Can fire-breathe from up to 4 tiles away.
.SH DUNGEON FEATURES
.TP
.B + (door)
Yellow = closed, red = locked, "/" = open.
Walk into a closed door to open it; locked doors need a key or \fBK\fPick.
.TP
.B # (secret door)
Looks like a wall until found with \fBS\fPearch.
.TP
.B ^ (trap)
Cyan=teleport, red=dart, yellow=pit, magenta=blind.
Traps are invisible until triggered.
.TP
.B $ (shop, green)
An in-level shop.  Press \fBs\fP while standing on it.
.TP
Dark rooms
Some rooms generate without lighting.  Visibility is limited to 2 tiles
unless you carry a lit torch (extends vision to 6 tiles).
.SH HUNGER
The player grows hungry as turns pass.
Status bar shows
.B Hungry
below 300 hunger points and
.B STARVING
at zero, at which point 1 HP is lost every 5 turns.
Eating food resets hunger to full.  Resting drains hunger slightly faster.
.SH SCORING
Your final score equals
.IR gold\ *\ 2\ +\ XP\ +\ dungeon_depth\ *\ 50 ,
plus 10\ 000 bonus points for winning.
.SH TIPS
.IP \(bu
Rest (\fBR\fP) between fights to recover, but watch your food supply.
.IP \(bu
Search (\fBS\fP) walls between rooms \(em secret doors often lead to
shortcuts or treasure.
.IP \(bu
A ring of invisibility stops monsters from waking by proximity; useful
for slipping past powerful enemies.
.IP \(bu
Enchant scrolls are rare \(em save them for your best weapon and armour.
.IP \(bu
Trolls regenerate; kill them quickly or they will recover mid-fight.
.IP \(bu
Dragons breathe fire at range.  Stay mobile or use a scroll of fireball.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.adahack_hiscore
High score table (plain text, created automatically on first play).
